{"id": "EUVD-2026-108293", "enisaUuid": "460849e8-cfb9-35e9-b5d1-ef23bfec865e", "description": "Incus 6.0.5 before 6.0.7, 6.12.0 before 7.0.2, and 7.1.0 before 7.5.0 contains a restriction bypass vulnerability that allows restricted project users to use pull mode migration via clustered refresh requests. Attackers with instance creation rights can send a refresh migration request for an existing instance to make the server open outbound TLS websocket connections and probe reachable services.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:41", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/lxc/incus/security/advisories/GHSA-443p-7392-h4v2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/incus-6.0.5-before-6.0.7-6.12.0-before-7.0.2-and-7.1.0-before-7.5.0-restricted-project-bypass-via-clustered-migration-refresh"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115370", "GHSA-7vwr-wj2h-fm66"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4c31f17e-e524-3bf4-887c-69150fa1c34d", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "7.1.0 <7.5.0"}, {"id": "4f4631e6-44e4-3405-94c4-76f37b525ff1", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "6.12.0 <7.0.2"}, {"id": "f9c8e537-e9f9-3b83-b9bf-8047b42c50d7", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "6.0.5 <6.0.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6980813a-e4ea-30d5-8169-a03349b9be0a", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}], "isExploited": false}